---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const title = 'Terms of Use';
const description = `The terms you accept by using ${SITE.name}: permitted use, accuracy disclaimers, intellectual property, and liability.`;
const updated = '2026-08-18';
const effective = 'August 18, 2026';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: `Terms of Use — ${SITE.name}`,
    url: new URL('/terms/', SITE.url).href,
    dateModified: updated,
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} updated={updated} schema={schema} ogType="article">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lede">Effective {effective}.</p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of {SITE.name} at{' '}
      <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a> — the index page for the Hunt Games
      network. By using the site you accept them. If you do not, please stop using the site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a free, independent directory of game wikis. It lists every site in the Hunt
      Games network — each one an independent, single-game reference published at its own
      subdomain — by genre, status, and domain. It is provided for informational purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Not affiliated with the games we cover</h2>
    <p>
      Neither this index nor any site in the Hunt Games network is affiliated with, endorsed by,
      sponsored by, or in any way officially connected to the developers or publishers of the games
      listed here. All game names, trademarks, logos, and assets referenced across the network are
      the property of their respective owners and are referred to under fair use for the purposes of
      commentary, criticism, and reference.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      We try to keep every listing on this index current — genre, status, and domain — but games and
      the sites that cover them change without notice. A site's status can move from "in survey" to
      live, a domain can change, and the content on any individual wiki is maintained separately from
      this index and may lag behind a patch or a release. Content is provided "as is" without
      warranty of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, fitness for a
      particular purpose, or non-infringement.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable regulation.</li>
      <li>
        Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site, its hosting infrastructure, or any connected
        system.
      </li>
      <li>
        Scrape, crawl, or otherwise access the site by automated means at a rate that degrades
        service for others.
      </li>
      <li>Republish substantial portions of the site's content as your own.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The original text, layout, code, and design of this index are ours. You're welcome to quote
      short passages with attribution and a link. Wholesale reproduction — including republishing the
      directory or feeding it into a product that reproduces it — requires permission.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Other sites in the network</h2>
    <p>
      Each subdomain linked from this index is a separately built and maintained site. It may carry
      its own terms of use, privacy policy, and disclaimers in addition to this page. This index
      links to them as a directory; it does not host, review, or take responsibility for their
      content beyond keeping the listing here accurate.
    </p>

    <h2>7. External links</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to third-party sites, including individual game storefronts and community
      resources referenced by network wikis. We do not control them and are not responsible for their
      content, availability, or practices. A link is not an endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} and its operators are not liable for any
      indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages arising from your use of, or inability
      to use, this site — including but not limited to reliance on information published here or on
      any linked site.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Availability</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided free of charge with no uptime commitment. We may change, suspend, or
      discontinue any part of it, including adding or removing entries, at any time and without
      notice.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these terms. The effective date above will change when we do. Continued use after
      a revision constitutes acceptance of it.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws applicable at the operator's place of establishment,
      without regard to conflict-of-law rules. If any provision is found unenforceable, the remainder
      stays in force.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, corrections, or intellectual property concerns:{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>. If you are a rights holder and
      believe something here exceeds fair use, contact us and we will address it promptly.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">These terms are written in plain language and are not legal advice.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
